sentences.text:
For the said reasons, the application is allowed and the applicant is directed to be released on bail in FIR No. 10/2022 dated 12.11.2022, under Sections 13(1) (c) (a) and 13(2) POC Act read with Sections 409/420/20-B IPC, registered at Police Station-ACB/New Delhi subject to the following conditions:
(a) The applicant shall furnish a personal bond in the sum of Rs. 25,000/-
(Rupees Twenty Five Thousand Only) with 01 surety in the like amount, to the satisfaction of the trial Court;
(b) The applicant shall not leave the country without permission of the trial Court and the order be communicated to Bureau of Immigration as well;
(c) The applicant shall surrender the passport to the trial Court and in case the applicant s passport has expired and he obtains a new passport, the same shall also be deposited with the trial Court;
Rajenderan Nair vs State Nct Of Delhi on 21 April, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/195433928/
